{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And the man's utterance:</b> As it says elsewhere, he is called גבר, likening Balaam to a rooster. Just as a rooster is adulterous above all, so Balaam had relations with his donkey. And just as a rooster knows the hours, so Balaam knew how to pinpoint the hour in which the Holy One, blessed be He, is angry. And just as a rooster's way is to stand on one leg, so Balaam limped on one of his legs."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:57.745705756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}